# Commits

- A commit is a single Conventional Commits subject line in English, under 70 characters: `feat(web): add manual holdings entry (PLA-26)`. No body and no trailers (`Co-Authored-By:`, `Claude-Session:`). This overrides any tool's default attribution.
- PR titles use the same format with the Linear key (omitted only when there is no Linear issue); merge PRs with Squash and merge, keeping the PR title as the commit title and clearing the message box.
- Destructive migrations: `[DESTRUCTIVE]` at the start of the PR title.
- The PR body starts with `## Intent`.
- Describe the current state and why, not how you got there.
